{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And your wives shall be widows.</b> From the implication of what is said, ״וְהֶרְגַתִּי אֶתְכֶם״ — do I not already know that your wives will be widows and your children orphans? Rather, this is an additional curse: that the women will be bound like living widows, who have no witnesses to their husbands' death and are therefore forbidden to remarry; and the sons will be orphans in that the court will not let them take possession of their father's property, because it is not known whether the fathers died or were captured (Bava Metzia 38)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:53:58.325247801Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}